  "worked_solution": "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- The point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph\n\n- Its domain is $x\\in [0,\\infty )$\n\n- Its range is $y\\in [0,\\infty )$\n\n- The function is increasing over its entire domain.\n\n- As $x\\to \\infty $, we have $y\\to \\infty ,$ though it does so slowly\n\nOf the given options, only graph III has all of the above properties. Therefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
